<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<rdf:RDF
   xmlns:owl="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#"
   xmlns:rdf="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#"
   xmlns:rdfs="http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#"
>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://w3id.org/hector/ontology#ArchaicForm">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept"/>
    <rdfs:comment>Classifies a Name as an archaic or obsolete form of a term.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:label>archaic form</rdfs:label>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://w3id.org/hector/ontology">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Ontology"/>
    <rdfs:comment>Terms HECTOR adds to Linked Art (CIDOC-CRM) for historical commodities, units of measure and customs rates. Term documentation lives here rather than in the JSON-LD context, which may only define terms. Namespace and URI policy: https://github.com/ihr-digital/hector/blob/main/docs/uri-policy.md</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:label>HECTOR vocabulary</rdfs:label>
    <owl:versionInfo>2026.10-alpha.1 (alpha pre-release, 2026-10-03): published for discussion, not for citation; terms, records and URIs may change or be withdrawn until the first full release</owl:versionInfo>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://w3id.org/hector/ontology#source">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#Property"/>
    <rdfs:comment>The source (for example a Book of Rates) that a Name or a Rate is taken from.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:label>source</rdfs:label>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://w3id.org/hector/ontology#quantityKind">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#Property"/>
    <rdfs:comment>The dimension a unit measures (mass, length, volume, count, package), given as a HECTOR unit dimension (unit/dimension/&lt;dim&gt;). May hold more than one value: a cask or a sack is both a measure and a package. A property, not part of the unit's URI: units are unit/&lt;slug&gt; (D7, 29 Sep 2026).</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:label>quantity kind</rdfs:label>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://w3id.org/hector/ontology#conversionToGram">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#Property"/>
    <rdfs:comment>The number of grams in one of this unit, as an xsd:decimal. State in the unit's description which definition of the unit the figure follows.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:label>conversion to gram</rdfs:label>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://w3id.org/hector/ontology#validThrough">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#Property"/>
    <rdfs:comment>The last year in which a Rate or a Name is attested or in force (xsd:gYear).</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:label>valid through</rdfs:label>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://w3id.org/hector/ontology#valueInPence">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#Property"/>
    <rdfs:comment>The exact value of a pre-decimal sterling amount in pence, as an xsd:decimal (a halfpenny is 0.5, a farthing 0.25). Pounds and shillings do not divide exactly into decimal pounds, so pence is the unit of record.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:label>value in pence</rdfs:label>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://w3id.org/hector/ontology#attestationCount">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#Property"/>
    <rdfs:comment>The number of times a commodity is attested in the London Customs Accounts corpus, as counted by that project's tagger (LCA docs/data/concept_attestation.json) when the record was exported; for a unit, the number of corpus spans the tagger typed as that unit (`unit` or `commodity-unit`).</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:label>attestation count</rdfs:label>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://w3id.org/hector/ontology#sourceText">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#Property"/>
    <rdfs:comment>The text of the source entry, verbatim.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:label>source text</rdfs:label>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://w3id.org/hector/ontology#Rate">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#Class"/>
    <rdfs:comment>A customs rate: the valuation or charge a Book of Rates sets on a quantity of a commodity for a period.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:label>Rate</rdfs:label>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://w3id.org/hector/ontology#definedAs">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#Property"/>
    <rdfs:comment>A quantity (a Linked Art Dimension: value and unit) that one of this unit is defined as or equal to, according to the source cited on the Dimension. Where sources disagree, each reading is a separate Dimension with its own source; a doubtful one says so in its note. Commodity-specific contents (a bale of cumin holds 3 cwt) are not definitions. Adopted 29 Sep 2026 (D7).</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:label>defined as</rdfs:label>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://w3id.org/hector/ontology#qualifier">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#Property"/>
    <rdfs:comment>A qualifier the source attaches to the goods a Rate is set on (origin, colour, quality, state, size), so that the rate applies to the commodity so qualified: 'Saffron of beyownd the se' is saffron, qualified as from overseas. Named in its modern form where the words are a spelling in the London Customs Accounts qualifier list, with its AAT concept (equivalent) or place (originPlace); otherwise in the source's words, classified as an attested variant.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:label>qualifier</rdfs:label>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://w3id.org/hector/ontology#amount">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#Property"/>
    <rdfs:comment>The MonetaryAmount of a Rate.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:label>amount</rdfs:label>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://w3id.org/hector/ontology#illustrative">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#Property"/>
    <rdfs:comment>True when a record is a worked example of HECTOR's shape rather than curated data. Its values are chosen to show the structure and must not be cited.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:label>illustrative</rdfs:label>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://w3id.org/hector/ontology#lsd">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#Property"/>
    <rdfs:comment>The amount as written in pounds, shillings and pence, for display.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:label>£ s d</rdfs:label>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://w3id.org/hector/ontology#originPlace">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#Property"/>
    <rdfs:comment>A place of origin or provenance associated with a commodity, or with a qualifier of one (Normandy, in Normandy canvas).</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:label>origin place</rdfs:label>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://w3id.org/hector/ontology#ModernLemma">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept"/>
    <rdfs:comment>Classifies the Name that is the modern standard form of a term.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:label>modern lemma</rdfs:label>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://w3id.org/hector/ontology#compoundOf">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#Property"/>
    <rdfs:comment>The simpler commodities a compound commodity is composed of. Also published by the London Customs Accounts glossary.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:label>compound of</rdfs:label>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://w3id.org/hector/ontology#perQuantity">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#Property"/>
    <rdfs:comment>The quantity (a Linked Art Dimension: value and unit) that a Rate's amount is charged on.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:label>per quantity</rdfs:label>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://w3id.org/hector/ontology#AttestedVariant">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept"/>
    <rdfs:comment>Classifies a Name as a variant form attested in a historical source.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:label>attested variant</rdfs:label>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://w3id.org/hector/ontology#historicalTerm">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#Property"/>
    <rdfs:comment>A historical word or phrase for a unit or commodity, where a full Name record is not warranted.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:label>historical term</rdfs:label>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://w3id.org/hector/ontology#validFrom">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#Property"/>
    <rdfs:comment>The year from which a Rate or a Name is attested or in force (xsd:gYear).</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:label>valid from</rdfs:label>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://w3id.org/hector/ontology#taxation">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#Property"/>
    <rdfs:comment>Links a commodity to a Rate set on it.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:label>taxation</rdfs:label>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://w3id.org/hector/ontology#phoneticKey">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#Property"/>
    <rdfs:comment>A phonetic transcription (IPA) of a Name, used to match variant spellings across sources.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:label>phonetic key</rdfs:label>
  </rdf:Description>
</rdf:RDF>
